 &\\sim \\text{mean } 0,\\ \\text{variance } 1 \\\\\n\\operatorname{Var}(q \\cdot k) &= \\sum_{i=1}^{d_k} \\operatorname{Var}(q_i k_i) = d_k \\\\\n\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\frac{q \\cdot k}{\\sqrt{d_k}}\\right) &= 1\n\\end{aligned}"}, "says": [{"id": "why-divide-by-the-square-root-of-d-k.1.1", "status": "ready", "text": "Assume the query and key components are independent, with mean zero and variance one, which is roughly what initialisation gives you.", "cues": [{"at": 11, "end": 35, "label": "query and key components", "target": "", "text": "q_i, k_i", "kind": "text", "t": 0.738}], "notes": [], "code": [], "audio": "audio/6b57880657f734aad14a8858.mp3", "duration": 8.7, "words": [{"s": 0.275, "e": 0.637, "c0": 0, "c1": 6}, {"s": 0.637, "e": 0.738, "c0": 7, "c1": 10}, {"s": 0.738, "e": 1.238, "c0": 11, "c1": 16}, {"s": 1.238, "e": 1.387, "c0": 17, "c1": 20}, {"s": 1.387, "e": 1.6, "c0": 21, "c1": 24}, {"s": 1.6, "e": 2.15, "c0": 25, "c1": 35}, {"s": 2.15, "e": 2.3, "c0": 36, "c1": 39}, {"s": 2.3, "e": 3.275, "c0": 40, "c1": 51}, {"s": 3.375, "e": 3.587, "c0": 53, "c1": 57}, {"s": 3.587, "e": 3.95, "c0": 58, "c1": 62}, {"s": 3.95, "e": 4.45, "c0": 63, "c1": 67}, {"s": 4.45, "e": 4.575, "c0": 68, "c1": 71}, {"s": 4.575, "e": 5.075, "c0": 72, "c1": 80}, {"s": 5.075, "e": 5.65, "c0": 81, "c1": 84}, {"s": 5.75, "e": 5.95, "c0": 86, "c1": 91}, {"s": 5.95, "e": 6.125, "c0": 92, "c1": 94}, {"s": 6.125, "e": 6.6, "c0": 95, "c1": 102}, {"s": 6.6, "e": 6.75, "c0": 103, "c1": 107}, {"s": 6.75, "e": 7.75, "c0": 108, "c1": 122}, {"s": 7.75, "e": 8.0, "c0": 123, "c1": 128}, {"s": 8.0, "e": 8.45, "c0": 129, "c1": 132}]}, {"id": "why-divide-by-the-square-root-of-d-k.2.1", "status": "ready", "text": "The dot product is a sum of d k such products, each with variance one. So the variance of the score is d k, and its spread grows like the square root of d k.", "cues": [{"at": 78, "end": 106, "label": "variance of the score is d k", "target": "", "text": "= d_k", "kind": "text", "t": 5.425}], "notes": [], "code": [], "audio": "audio/f6afff82a2cf7422fa2705fb.mp3", "duration": 10.775, "words": [{"s": 0.25, "e": 0.325, "c0": 0, "c1": 3}, {"s": 0.325, "e": 0.575, "c0": 4, "c1": 7}, {"s": 0.575, "e": 1.05, "c0": 8, "c1": 15}, {"s": 1.05, "e": 1.163, "c0": 16, "c1": 18}, {"s": 1.163, "e": 1.262, "c0": 19, "c1": 20}, {"s": 1.262, "e": 1.462, "c0": 21, "c1": 24}, {"s": 1.462, "e": 1.587, "c0": 25, "c1": 27}, {"s": 1.587, "e": 1.837, "c0": 28, "c1": 29}, {"s": 1.837, "e": 2.15, "c0": 30, "c1": 31}, {"s": 2.15, "e": 2.375, "c0": 32, "c1": 36}, {"s": 2.375, "e": 3.15, "c0": 37, "c1": 45}, {"s": 3.288, "e": 3.562, "c0": 47, "c1": 51}, {"s": 3.562, "e": 3.725, "c0": 52, "c1": 56}, {"s": 3.725, "e": 4.2, "c0": 57, "c1": 65}, {"s": 4.2, "e": 4.95, "c0": 66, "c1": 69}, {"s": 5.125, "e": 5.325, "c0": 71, "c1": 73}, {"s": 5.325, "e": 5.425, "c0": 74, "c1": 77}, {"s": 5.425, "e": 5.938, "c0": 78, "c1": 86}, {"s": 5.938, "e": 6.013, "c0": 87, "c1": 89}, {"s": 6.013, "e": 6.1, "c0": 90, "c1": 93}, {"s": 6.1, "e": 6.45, "c0": 94, "c1": 99}, {"s": 6.45, "e": 6.612, "c0": 100, "c1": 102}, {"s": 6.612, "e": 6.862, "c0": 103, "c1": 104}, {"s": 6.862, "e": 7.475, "c0": 105, "c1": 106}, {"s": 7.575, "e": 7.688, "c0": 108, "c1": 111}, {"s": 7.688, "e": 7.8, "c0": 112, "c1": 115}, {"s": 7.8, "e": 8.15, "c0": 116, "c1": 122}, {"s": 8.15, "e": 8.625, "c0": 123, "c1": 128}, {"s": 8.625, "e": 8.787, "c0": 129, "c1": 133}, {"s": 8.787, "e": 8.887, "c0": 134, "c1": 137}, {"s": 8.887, "e": 9.25, "c0": 138, "c1": 144}, {"s": 9.25, "e": 9.5, "c0": 145, "c1": 149}, {"s": 9.5, "e": 9.625, "c0": 150, "c1": 152}, {"s": 9.625, "e": 9.838, "c0": 153, "c1": 154}, {"s": 9.838, "e": 10.55, "c0": 155, "c1": 157}]}, {"id": "why-divide-by-the-square-root-of-d-k.3.1", "status": "ready", "text": "Dividing by the square root of d k brings the variance back to one, no matter how wide the model is.", "cues": [{"at": 46, "end": 66, "label": "variance back to one", "target": "", "text": "= 1", "kind"